<Base title="Research | GenATK" description="How GenATK evaluates and publishes evidence about deterministic procedural generation.">
  <article>
    <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
    <h1>Evidence before articles.</h1>
    <p class="lede">GenATK publishes research artifacts only when their methods, limitations, and intended use can be explained clearly.</p>
    <p>Future studies may include reproducible seed sets, export checks, benchmarks, and practical worksheets. Each article that relies on one will link directly to its public evidence and describe what it does not prove.</p>
    <ul class="card-list">
      <li>
        <h2><a href="/research/asset-review-record/">Asset review record</a></h2>
        <p>A tool-agnostic worksheet for connecting a reviewed output to the inputs and export that were actually checked.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Explore the related <a href="/labs/seeded-assets/">seeded asset lab</a>, the <a href="/learn/">learning library</a>, or our <a href="/about/">editorial approach</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
